I go over to the shoe department and sit down on a bench.
My feet are always cold here in Denmark.
A friendly shop assistant comes over to me.
"Excuse me, I am looking for some warm brown boots," I say.
"Yes, one moment," she says.
"What shoe size do you take?"
"I take size thirty-nine," I reply.
She fetches a pair of beautiful boots for me.
I put them on.
They are some very heavy shoes.
But they are also incredibly warm.
I stand up and walk around the shop a bit.
My toes feel fantastic.
"They fit perfectly," I say to the assistant.
On a small table next to the bench, there are woolen socks.
I take two pairs of thick socks with me.
Now I am completely ready for snow and frost.
